        "messageOrdinal": 352,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-05-12",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "12 May 1846",
        "text": "And all those strange people moving about like phantoms of life.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s8686",
        "messageOrdinal": 425,
        "sender": "Robert",
        "date": "1846-06-27",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "27 June 1846",
        "text": "How could I presume, for one thing, to hope for last evening’s letter ... a pure piece of kindness in you, Ba!",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
